[[0,1338503,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-11T01:02:20","Hitlore","",[],"","Saint Anita Going Against the Narrative","http://i.imgur.com/bt1Qzsr.jpg","NeoFAG"],[1,6533936,0,0,0,0,"2016-10-11T01:26:19","Indepentarian","[e]",[],"<p>Well fuck me, go Anita. Broken clock, and all that. </p>\n<p>She shoulda gotten a Jones shirt and tried for that $5k. </p>"],[1,6534084,0,6,0,6,"2016-10-11T01:48:00","Gafsucks","",[],"<p>Sadly image is fake. Would have been funny tho. </p>"],[2,6534434,6534084,1,0,1,"2016-10-11T02:54:07","Indepentarian","",[],"<p>:(</p>\n<p>Guess it was too good to be true. </p>"],[1,6534624,0,2,0,2,"2016-10-11T03:27:34","DerVarg","",[],"<p>Bitch neeeds to take some of that swindled money and get a fucking nose job.</p>"],[1,6534664,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-11T03:34:03","gucciballsack","",[],"<p>I'd rape her any day tbh</p>"],[1,6534668,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-11T03:34:54","JohnnyPhatsaqs","",[],"<p>I'd fuck her. Easily. </p>"],[1,6536359,0,0,0,0,"2016-10-11T11:55:34","Freedom_Against_GAF","",[],"<p><a href=\"https://twitter.com/RejZoRSheep/status/785505962081869827\">Exploitable image is posted</a> on Twitter. Go nuts!</p>"],[1,6538339,0,0,0,0,"2016-10-11T17:01:54","SyntheticWatermelon","",[],"<p>All that money and she can't afford pants without cum all over them.</p>"]]
[[0,1338504,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-11T01:02:24","consciouslybinocular","",[],"<p>Our breadboard prototyping tool METABOARD was recently accepted into the Telstra muru-d accelerator Interview Round. We hope it will help bring software developers further into the fold of electronics.</p>\n<p>When I am simulating a circuit on breadboard, I notice, as the complexity of the circuit increases, I have to manually manage a mess of peripheral components and wiring. To solve this problem, I want to build a device that augments the breadboard to replace peripheral components and wire with programmatic internal components.</p>\n<p>On top of this function, I want the device to route each pin to all other pins, so I can reconfigure and check all pins of the same value simultaneously with high level software interfaces such as Arduino.</p>\n<p>I also want to download and share my designs with other developers without having to document or illustrate the arrangement and configuration of components.</p>\n<p>At present, we require funds to finalise design and mass produce this device, but we have already built a working prototype that demonstrates its utility.</p>\n<p>If you interested, check out this video of our first working prototype <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2D-xQ0YyXPIYouTube\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2D-xQ0YyXPIYouTube</a> or ask questions below. For early users, we have launched a Indiegogo today: <a href=\"https://igg.me/at/themetaboard\">https://igg.me/at/themetaboard</a></p>","We are giving software developers programmatic control over their breadboards","","electronics"]]
